The test builds `indexes_coords` as a dict literal with keys in insertion order: `x`, `y`, `z`, `w`, `v`. In `decompose_interp`, the loop iterates over `indexes_coords.items()` in that same order and immediately adds the current pair with `partial_indexes_coords.update([index_coords])`. The code also yields and resets `partial_indexes_coords` whenever the accumulated destination dims are disjoint from the remaining ones. Using the test dims, `x`/`y` form one group, then the dict is reset, and `z`, `w`, `v` accumulate into the next group. So at the 5th iteration (`i == 4`), right after the update, the keys in `partial_indexes_coords` are `z`, `w`, `v`.

## Answer
{"iteration_number":5,"partial_indexes_coords_keys":["z","w","v"]}
